# Declarative Rust crates to cross-compile for all arches in B19_RUST_CROSS_TARGETS.
# Format: <crate@version> (one per line)
# Only works with musl variant (B19_RUST_LIBC=musl).
# Binary name is discovered from cargo install output (crate name may differ from binary).
# Output: ${CARGO_INSTALL_ROOT}/bin/<binary>.<arch> (e.g. fd.amd64, fd.arm64, fd.riscv64).
# Used to break OS-layer bootstrap cycles — downstream consumers pick the right arch binary.

# Example: cross-compile fd for amd64, arm64, riscv64 (musl static)
# fd-find@10.1.0

# Example: cross-compile ripgrep for all supported arches
# ripgrep@14.1.0

# Example: cross-compile a custom crate
# my-crate@1.0.0